inside the second outer invocation:\n\n- `git -C /Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/kit-source rev-parse HEAD` — exit 0; 2026-09-10T17:24:23.748449+00:00.\n\n- `/Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/acceptance-pr-20260910/reviews/f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766/adversarial/uv-cache/builds-v0/.tmpZa1hLe/bin/python -B scripts/devkit/kit_doctor.py --root /Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/acceptance-pr-20260910/reviews/f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766/adversarial/mut-adversarial-f770f183-p3r4tuqp/repo --manifest /Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/kit-source/kit-manifest.json --json` — exit 0; 2026-09-10T17:24:23.813814+00:00.\n\n- `/Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/acceptance-pr-20260910/reviews/f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766/adversarial/uv-cache/builds-v0/.tmpZa1hLe/bin/python -B scripts/devkit/kit_doctor.py --root /Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/acceptance-pr-20260910/reviews/f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766/adversarial/mut-adversarial-f770f183-p3r4tuqp/repo --adapter-report --adapter-source /Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/kit-source --json` — exit 0; 2026-09-10T17:24:23.865916+00:00.\n\n- `/Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/acceptance-pr-20260910/reviews/f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766/adversarial/uv-cache/builds-v0/.tmpZa1hLe/bin/python -B scripts/devkit/check_doc_budget.py` — exit 0; 2026-09-10T17:24:23.899758+00:00.\n\n- `bash -n scripts/devkit/dev_session.sh` — exit 0; 2026-09-10T17:24:23.904495+00:00.\n\n- `bash -n scripts/devkit/reconcile_sessions.sh` — exit 0; 2026-09-10T17:24:23.908281+00:00.\n\n- `bash -n scripts/devkit/lib/repo_root.sh` — exit 0; 2026-09-10T17:24:23.911218+00:00.\n\n- `bash -n scripts/devkit/hooks/pre-push` — exit 0; 2026-09-10T17:24:23.914371+00:00.\n\n- `sh -n init.sh` — exit 0; 2026-09-10T17:24:23.921483+00:00.\n\n\nAudit output and exact argv/cwd/date records: [audit-results.json](/Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/acceptance-pr-20260910/reviews/f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766/adversarial/mut-adversarial-f770f183-p3r4tuqp/evidence/audit-results.json).\n\n**Mutation-test new branches.** The driver retrieved original target bytes with `git show f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766:<path>`, saved them, applied one mutation, re-read the target, asserted the exact intended replacement, and retained the unified diff before testing. After every case, its `finally` block restored the original bytes and checked equality plus SHA-256 before proceeding. The stored manifest was never regenerated or edited.\n\nEach test command explicitly selected `scripts/devkit/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_kit_repo_self_check_is_clean` and then used `-m 'not driftcheck'`. Every run reports **1 deselected**, so the exclusion demonstrably removed a test. The failures below are behavioral assertions, not checksum or stored-text comparisons.\n\n| Mutation | Behavioral result | Restoration |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ignore test-path symlinks | `test_installed_test_targets_refuse_declared_symlink` and `...symlinked_ancestor` fail because ValueError was not raised; **2 failed, 5 passed, 1 deselected; exit 1** | Exact original bytes restored |\n| Accept missing test modules | `test_installed_test_targets_and_main_refuse_a_declared_missing_module` fails because ValueError was not raised; **1 failed, 6 passed, 1 deselected; exit 1** | Exact original bytes restored |\n| Replace state-file content hashing with a constant | Six `test_guard_catches_a_write_into_real_state[...overwrite]` cases fail because the leaking inner pytest process exits 0; **6 failed, 41 passed, 1 deselected; exit 1** | Exact original bytes restored |\n\nAll three mutants were behaviorally killed. These mutations validate the named properties only; they do not cover the state-root finding.\n\n\nMutation `runner-symlink-guard`:\n\n```diff\n--- f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766:scripts/devkit/run_installed_tests.py\n+++ mutant:scripts/devkit/run_installed_tests.py\n@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@\n         current = root\n         for part in installed_rel.parts:\n             current /= part\n-            if current.is_symlink():\n+            if False:  # review mutation: ignore symlink ancestry\n                 raise ValueError(\n                     f\"declared test path crosses a symlink after engine remapping: {rel}\"\n                 )\n```\n\nExact inner test command, executed beneath the serial wrapper:\n\n```sh\n/Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/acceptance-pr-20260910/reviews/f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766/adversarial/uv-cache/builds-v0/.tmpZa1hLe/bin/python -B -m pytest scripts/devkit/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_installed_test_targets_use_manifest_not_directory_contents scripts/devkit/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_installed_test_main_invokes_pytest_and_propagates_failure scripts/devkit/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_installed_test_main_reports_a_successful_empty_suite scripts/devkit/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_installed_test_targets_and_main_refuse_a_declared_missing_module scripts/devkit/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_installed_test_targets_skip_a_declined_missing_test_root scripts/devkit/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_installed_test_targets_refuse_declared_symlink scripts/devkit/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_installed_test_targets_refuse_declared_symlinked_ancestor scripts/devkit/tests/test_kit_doctor.py::test_kit_repo_self_check_is_clean -m 'not driftcheck' -q\n```\n\nCwd `/Users/topi/Coding/adk-field-exercises/item5-b-20260909/acceptance-pr-20260910/reviews/f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766/adversarial/mut-adversarial-f770f183-p3r4tuqp/repo`; reviewed revision `f770f183bf6691f1f706c676b740cf2ef5ceb766` plus the displayed mutation; date `2026-09-10T17:24:40.791088+00:00`; exit 1. Raw result: [runner-symlink-guard.log](/Users/topi/C